#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161772 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "59ea7ebb-5b69-5551-a5b9-c286e2730881" :question/math-academy-id "e-8160" :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](images/e1/e104f037293e19fe2a12d9b2e14cc344d5cca06f933f393755cf03568b5702c0.png)  Evaluate the function when ![](images/88/8832f5ec6073de4098b3b0f856a3ab5e000926a9d09f76e87909adb67777cc17.png)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](images/4c/4c5ce198c2271b51807f4c17fffdf4288c524ff73469196bd481dc489c5a0e40.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161773 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "30204c69-3362-5cc1-a04a-3bb83559b300" :question/math-academy-id "e-8161" :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](images/dc/dcea1a36972408a1f6a56577f61150bd8e4c2b91284820ca47c632a985d912ca.png) and ![](images/f9/f9885ea740945a64e44931aca4befbd4022a84ae0fa1454627f2b44133eb4651.png)" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](images/65/652258046237288de7102e402a266dd3afff1abfecf97aa2156a351a7611afb3.png) and ![](images/58/58ef5fbadaf595035dc902aac9b66bbce61fea79b6a4144ed060f0486dda982c.png) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161774 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "34398117-07f4-51d9-a879-30a0f6891e68" :question/math-academy-id "e-8162" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4dfdcd2e2f0d80ee8b6633b0dd4bc33b477b22e4db0f2ad36cbfa62eef702659.png)\nConsider the matrix ![](images/15/15fa693fff5bc0eb2a8851089612b5a3fb969c3fd5fbc7c0821e58e52ff4260d.png) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](images/7c/7c7f59284956b7a02d9d9d16387cfba529479fb49aa8efff3bfa908be0fbb04f.png) in terms of the components of ![](images/ed/ed54028979894fad0ac2b928c90c9eeea9361d1c8514fb61ee8ce28435ac2a5c.png) and ![](images/98/9849708035aaa18397dfafbbcdfeb923f576296406c494c30093477f6b2aaa33.png)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](images/e8/e8f54943816e5af3ad7a3b92ff68887d8126962ffcba1d3109d10390616d8a04.png) of ![](images/33/3397629141c3034fbd4b5cd5bd8c554676175a4b1e3f5eccd26cc5d66ee1bec8.png) corresponds to the term ![](images/e4/e4b6d1207e1c34e37c760af85eb4a4e5594e3db2da2c4ba4841a4106de188c1b.png) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](images/73/734889027df1469d75a4506f295a277b908081224b5860ebf9ec8ea432053dd9.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](images/4c/4ccd64cd17dd595c826e5a8bf13d4bf991c57d128d7a3fbca5a49eaf265f0867.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161775 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "84e1b597-45d7-51f4-aaa9-8a52c753a510" :question/math-academy-id "e-8163" :question/problem "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](images/24/24b1e29dccdff51c2ca2c7780a8a5dfcf9c74ed91d48afdde8a14c5127f89ce1.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b71e7f5-e589-5173-b8d1-5bca4549c39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269660} {:answer/id #uuid "47b1a8af-7aea-532c-8d7e-ec9ca4a680a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269919} {:answer/id #uuid "8edbc905-d6c8-5d53-b939-9b29819d4197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270508} {:answer/id #uuid "b07da744-4817-52a4-9472-01482b684293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270842} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a6607f-78a6-5636-bb3a-99fd1012c614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b71e7f5-e589-5173-b8d1-5bca4549c39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269660} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf57b9b-e627-50e0-b1ee-e1548d6dfec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7a2955a-d0ed-5f0b-a82c-5ef03bbf9550" :question/math-academy-id "q-140851" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e179630-a47a-54c8-a994-33d07597762f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269521} {:answer/id #uuid "3592eac6-b1b2-514f-b1c0-230e4d054819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269759} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbb606b-d502-546a-9c9b-7f1f84ba1bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269988} {:answer/id #uuid "839850ab-34ae-5253-8727-21e3f2303e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270406} {:answer/id #uuid "a270baaf-98f0-5ed4-a01e-9d526d00752b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3592eac6-b1b2-514f-b1c0-230e4d054819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269759} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7b09c8-3189-5ed7-afb9-4ecd048bffce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1823b0b-dd9b-5b00-861c-14c6a4bab473" :question/math-academy-id "q-140853" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e110b97-5ab5-5617-aa1a-9f75fa92ce22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269391} {:answer/id #uuid "284ebe93-9d33-5b44-86a9-d99931234376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269630} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9dfa71-ca6b-59de-8143-11e3be4e3df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269943} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ba7f9a-5b96-5112-9756-284a5a5f9e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270872} {:answer/id #uuid "d8197c76-cd41-58f6-8a5a-d3b5c0bf37ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e110b97-5ab5-5617-aa1a-9f75fa92ce22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269391} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac61f25-e40e-52f8-bb85-65ad8a3cc3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "806f88a5-c472-5e05-ba98-6e9ea06c0751" :question/math-academy-id "q-140861" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 20\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b45b4bc3-eafb-5318-aaf2-06db9573422c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + x_{2}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160833} {:answer/id #uuid "e909e9f9-9fa0-5bd4-8101-5e1478df4dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{1}y_{1} - 2x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{1} - x_{2}y_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160834} {:answer/id #uuid "008980ff-a29a-5ace-a587-da597c83acd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{1}y_{1} - 2x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160835} {:answer/id #uuid "1a9c215c-b0e3-54c1-b1bc-3c4316046876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{1} + 2x_{2}y_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160836} {:answer/id #uuid "6e59ecfe-2975-5bea-be52-eb553bca660a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{1}y_{1} + 2x_{1}y_{2} - 2x_{2}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160837}] :answer-field/id #uuid "89c44a10-398e-5901-bd28-38e9099fece6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160832}] :question/id #uuid "734f0c5e-0d8c-5660-90a8-1dd3058abdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-93684" :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form $x^{T}Ay$ in terms of the components of $x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $y = \\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065d3589-3788-5175-ad2e-ca115572f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354707} {:answer/id #uuid "67df311e-165a-597e-b288-ad0f5f0b6045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355584} {:answer/id #uuid "a193fd48-d649-5aa5-9966-9c43b7ea4461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356102} {:answer/id #uuid "a3379ff6-3b09-55dd-bf18-e79be3b7a15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356110} {:answer/id #uuid "d78cb865-9e7f-5234-9e23-e2cf29601927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67df311e-165a-597e-b288-ad0f5f0b6045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355584} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3a5fb3-8ee9-561c-b9ce-d7ccb5a0bd22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82537968-6767-565c-820b-eb7ee2eb1460" :question/math-academy-id "q-93685" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+(-1)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34791725-9520-5f7a-ab6c-9218c24779dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355129} {:answer/id #uuid "8360267f-4c94-52e2-add6-b66758050ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355822} {:answer/id #uuid "864a7748-78b9-5775-a445-8883818a7bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218